  "body": "**Replaces #433** (opened from the old fork, which can no longer take pushes). Same head commit; nothing else changed.\n\n**Stacked on #432 (#416).** Part of #363.\n\n## What changed\n**With the G76 cycle post option, the G76 words now describe the passes the verdict judged.**\n- The record maps 1:1: `G76 P(m)(r)(a) Q(dmin) R(d)` / `G76 X Z P(k) Q(dd) F`, where:\n  - dd = the first pass's depth;\n  - dmin = the step (constant depth) or the plan's minimum (constant area);\n  - d = the finishing pass's own depth;\n  - m = 1 + spring passes;\n  - a = twice the flank angle.\n- **Control model** (GSK988TA, Fanuc-compatible G76):\n  - each roughing pass goes to `max(dd·√n, previous + dmin)`, up to k − d;\n  - the first finishing pass cuts d, and m − 1 more repeat at k;\n  - each pass starts `depth·tan(a/2)` along Z.\n- **Refused by name with G76 chosen:** alternating infeed (the CL carries a new `alternating` flag; `ALT 1` is written to the stream only when set), a doubled angle outside 0/29/30/55/60/80 (so 29.5° is refused), and a one-pass thread.\n\n**⚠ This changes posted output for the default G76 thread: `R0` becomes `R0.4`.** The golden `fanuc-lathe/thread_g76.nc` changes on one line: `G76 P010000 Q400 R0` → `G76 P010000 Q400 R0.4`.\n- Why: with `R0` the control roughs 0.4, 0.8 and 1.2, then cuts its finishing pass at the root again. That is a fourth full-depth pass the verdict never judged. It's not a gouge, but it isn't what was verified.\n- With `R0.4` it roughs 0.4 and 0.8 and finishes at 1.2: exactly the three passes we judge.\n- Making `R0` true instead would have meant changing G32 output and the judged passes.\n- Note: the #363 research said Q = infeed made the control cut a decreasing ladder. That isn't so, because dmin = infeed clamps every step equal. The real gap was R.\n\n`docs/decisions/417-g76-matches-verified.md`\n\n## How tested\n- New app `lathe_post_g76_schedule` (4 tests):\n  - a new flank, constant-area golden `thread_g76_area.nc` (`G76 P020055 Q100 R0.05` / `G76 X9.6 Z14 P1200 Q400 F2`): the control's schedule computed from the posted words matches the laid depths and stations within 1 µm;\n  - the default (`R0.4`) and a 0.5 step (`Q500 R0.2`) also match;\n  - one refusal per unexpressible option;\n  - `ALT` survives the stream and the project file.\n- Existing post, cl, inverted_post, lathe_post, golden_cl, project_roundtrip, tool_law, tool_gate and commands_undo suites are green.\n- `clippy --tests -D warnings` (cl, post, motion, app, ui) is clean.\n- The gate escalated to batch (cl changed). It fails only on tests already red on main: headless GPU, #415, and `swarf_pose_continuity` (PR #351).\n\n## Not exercised / not confirmed by sources (draft until a lathe sim or machine run)\n1. Which way Fanuc shifts Z per pass for flank infeed. This follows LinuxCNC's sign; either sign is gouge-safe.\n2. Whether the control also shifts each pass's end Z. If not, early passes end up to k·tan θ off at the runout, shallower than the root.\n3. How the minimum-depth clamp applies (read as a per-pass minimum, per the manual's definition).\n4. Micron rounding of the words: the control's ladder can differ by under 1 µm.\n\nNone of these moves the finished thread form.\n\nChangelog: G76 threading output states the passes that were verified: the finish allowance R is posted (default threads now post R0.4 instead of R0), and options G76 cannot express are refused by name (#417)\n\nFixes #417\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
